# yosys area/timing metrics flow (frozen harness file).
# Memories are collected but NOT decomposed into FFs; their bits are counted
# separately and credited as SRAM-macro area (see scoring.py).
# One ltp report is emitted on the final mapped netlist (the scored one).
# The former pre-abc informational ltp was dropped: on ~2M-cell designs
# with structural pseudo-loops (measured 9.5M loop warnings on one solver
# design) ltp's cycle analysis dominated synth wall-time, and levels_rtl
# (its only unique output) is informational -- evaluate.py parses it as 0
# when absent. abc runs with -fast: exhaustive abc takes
# hours on a realistic-scale design (~500k cells), which would make every
# evaluation unfinishable; -fast maps every submission with the same
# effort, so NE/levels stay comparable (slightly conservative for all).
# Invoked by evaluate.py with {FILES}/{MACROS} substituted into a temp copy.
read_verilog -sv {FILES}
hierarchy -check -top msh_chip_top
proc
log === per-module stats (pre-flatten, module-structure metrics) ===
stat -json
flatten
opt_expr
opt_clean
stat -json
memory -nomap
opt -fast
techmap
opt -fast
abc -fast -g AND,NAND,OR,NOR,XOR,XNOR,ANDNOT,ORNOT,MUX
opt_clean
stat
stat -json
# macro instances stay blackboxed; dump just their cells + parameters for
# pricing (a full-netlist write_json hit 672 MB on a 2.19M-cell design)
tee -o {MACROS} dump t:msh_sram t:msh_rom
log === scored longest path (final mapped netlist) ===
ltp -noff
